nal market data responsibly, including how to choose surveys, match jobs, age data, and avoid false precision.", "children": [{"id": "d8b76622-9071-4a53-8fcd-36dbfef7306d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Compensation surveys", "children": [{"id": "d447998e-dda7-4c53-be72-21aa436faf71", "type": "concept", "title": "survey scope"}, {"id": "41a2cde7-1d87-4e69-a702-27527fea1d3e", "type": "concept", "title": "participant mix"}, {"id": "df715472-3531-47a2-ba55-2a8fd69c3419", "type": "concept", "title": "job matching"}, {"id": "9feda4d2-1f1c-4afd-a0ef-a76f221b29e4", "type": "concept", "title": "sample size"}, {"id": "e03502e1-43b7-4c63-84ba-49099e6efd64", "type": "concept", "title": "published cuts"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students how salary surveys are built and how to judge whether data are appropriate for a specific role or labor market."}, {"id": "8f60dd2c-1b92-4ebd-b23b-d4a92540c5d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Market pricing workflow", "children": [{"id": "e7fc5d03-e059-4056-ab01-024c39579b73", "type": "concept", "title": "benchmark jobs"}, {"id": "f662f86a-553a-4047-a2b8-8921aaa19c0a", "type": "concept", "title": "percentiles"}, {"id": "8483d62e-a05a-4197-a150-cf01479d9919", "type": "concept", "title": "data aging"}, {"id": "225eda12-eeb0-4b90-99d6-6399550f2331", "type": "concept", "title": "geographic differentials"}, {"id": "a0dfc1bd-c4fd-41bf-b6c0-3f2ae2a36694", "type": "concept", "title": "blended market rates"}], "description": "Students practice turning raw market data into usable pay recommendations."}, {"id": "f4daaf52-dbdd-48a4-9739-92f891f2214b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data quality and ethics", "children": [{"id": "eed0c9db-d3e2-4970-80e8-4debc7c212c6", "type": "concept", "title": "data recency"}, {"id": "36c8461d-4c66-49a8-a6d3-45e9172aecc4", "type": "concept", "title": "outliers"}, {"id": "94b8ea5a-bce5-4856-a917-eab6a5bd6a47", "type": "concept", "title": "confidentiality"}, {"id": "a1a24ea4-2627-4f6e-8412-91fbba8982aa", "type": "concept", "title": "antitrust caution"}, {"id": "a5b57348-6a9a-4e25-aa33-1451a97927e4", "type": "concept", "title": "vendor governance"}], "description": "Students learn why compensation data can mislead and why confidentiality, antitrust boundaries, and data governance matter."}]}, {"id": "7c125c33-fa00-448d-bb6c-48138eba2ae5", "type": "topic", "title": "Base Pay Structures, Grades, and Ranges", "description": "This unit shows how organizations turn strategy, job value, and market data into structured pay systems that managers can administer consistently.", "children": [{"id": "79890eff-a439-4f3b-82ae-1878a6afb2ac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pay grades and bands", "children": [{"id": "deac541b-72ca-4c79-9782-67bd3b684812", "type": "concept", "title": "traditional grades"}, {"id": "12a03cd3-7636-4fa4-97ad-0d71c086cead", "type": "concept", "title": "broadbanding"}, {"id": "dd78396f-ed4b-4046-9e82-6f418e7e31fa", "type": "concept", "title": "career bands"}, {"id": "bea23620-6734-4046-9139-43e6b67bed56", "type": "concept", "title": "grade overlap"}, {"id": "58168dd4-a08d-4fbb-9ae4-993e04a8e2c4", "type": "concept", "title": "control points"}], "description": "Students learn how jobs are grouped into pay grades or broader bands and what each structure enables or constrains."}, {"id": "1012aa72-4e7f-4973-a551-9a7e172c29fa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Range design", "children": [{"id": "3922ef3a-65a0-429b-85fd-0f4e5b10bea4", "type": "concept", "title": "range minimum"}, {"id": "2569b348-f394-4f47-814a-b872000aae7c", "type": "concept", "title": "midpoint"}, {"id": "acc91e87-4eda-4290-a2f7-5c09b1f3aa1b", "type": "concept", "title": "range maximum"}, {"id": "792f959a-2643-4d14-a04f-71181999fef3", "type": "concept", "title": "range spread"}, {"id": "8d4e089a-f771-45f4-bcb8-b6aed105315e", "type": "concept", "title": "midpoint differential"}], "description": "The class covers minimums, midpoints, maximums, spreads, and midpoint progressions."}, {"id": "e4f9e8b6-8cac-4eb