ncept", "title": "remote-work adjustments"}, {"id": "4c1c4226-dcea-42d9-b77c-e166f1251582", "type": "concept", "title": "locality premiums"}], "description": "Students compare location-based pay, national ranges, and hybrid models."}, {"id": "22f116a6-f55e-4ac1-87df-56dfd593157d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global rewards", "children": [{"id": "d0ef767f-7b6f-472d-88a5-8250b2b547db", "type": "concept", "title": "country norms"}, {"id": "8fc5e38f-1625-4a06-a315-00940723f3a1", "type": "concept", "title": "statutory benefits"}, {"id": "73d89106-f481-498f-a0f2-e5cfe1d70050", "type": "concept", "title": "expatriate allowances"}, {"id": "e2666350-73b9-4564-acdf-bef0f3877b44", "type": "concept", "title": "currency and tax issues"}, {"id": "44ba559d-6843-41e7-b801-68f1a0062b53", "type": "concept", "title": "global grading"}], "description": "The course introduces cross-border compensation and benefits issues without assuming one U.S.-centric model fits all contexts."}, {"id": "c53b8ca1-1943-4970-987c-83933b2af9b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Flexible and alternative work arrangements", "children": [{"id": "a853f3b6-9820-4d6e-8fbf-28889ec5de23", "type": "concept", "title": "part-time benefits"}, {"id": "26eba50f-da23-4031-a0e3-d0b96271951c", "type": "concept", "title": "contractor classification"}, {"id": "e42d2f1c-b9e8-4944-95d1-5a574ccb2877", "type": "concept", "title": "schedule flexibility"}, {"id": "94992e2b-b4fa-42a0-858f-1487ca6f7844", "type": "concept", "title": "shift differentials"}, {"id": "e4eb15e1-484e-400f-be93-b7104f640901", "type": "concept", "title": "contingent workforce risk"}], "description": "Students consider how rewards apply to part-time, gig, contract, and flexible workers."}]}, {"id": "48d2cb25-3765-45f0-8af6-31e1cc6be4a3", "type": "topic", "title": "Compensation Analytics and Rewards Case", "description": "The capstone unit asks students to diagnose a rewards problem, analyze data, weigh tradeoffs, and communicate a defensible recommendation."